{"type": "assistant", "message": {"model": "claude-sonnet-5-5", "id": "msg_011CfbfvpKFKHCYf6ccgetx8", "type": "message", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "`git rebase --onto <newbase> <upstream> [<branch>]` replays the commits that are in `<branch>` but not in `<upstream>` on top of `<newbase>`. Plain `git rebase` can only move a branch onto the upstream it was forked from. `--onto` lets you pick the new base and the cut point separately.\n\n**Example: move a branch off another feature branch**\n\nYou branched `feature-b` from `feature-a`, but `feature-a` isn't ready. You want `feature-b` to sit directly on `main`:\n\n```\nmain:       A---B\n                 \\\nfeature-a:        C---D\n                       \\\nfeature-b:              E---F\n```\n\n```bash\ngit rebase --onto main feature-a feature-b\n```\n\n- `main` is the new base.\n- `feature-a` is the old base. Commits reachable from it (C, D) are excluded.\n- `feature-b` is the branch to move. It defaults to the current branch.\n\nResult:\n\n```\nmain:       A---B---E'---F'\n                \\\nfeature-a:       C---D\n```\n\nE and F are replayed as new commits E' and F' with new hashes. `feature-a` is untouched.\n\n**Other common uses**\n\n- **Drop commits from the middle or start of a branch:** `git rebase --onto A~3 A~1` removes the commits between those two points.\n- **Transplant a range:** `git rebase --onto main abc123 def456` moves only the commits after `abc123` up to `def456`.\n\nIf you've already pushed the branch, rebasing rewrites its history, so you'll need `git push --force-with-lease` afterward."}], "container": null, "stop_reason": null, "stop_sequence": null, "stop_details": null, "usage": {"input_tokens": 2, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 7222, "cache_read_input_tokens": 16780, "cache_creation": {"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 7222}, "output_tokens": 8, "service_tier": "standard", "inference_geo": "not_available"}, "input_transformations": [], "diagnostics": null, "context_management": null}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "session_id": "ed89c43a-6ba5-47e0-aa90-60cb74011af9", "uuid": "38e9bbce-b05d-4819-9318-bc0e6ef9bc69", "timestamp": "2026-10-01T14:26:10.754Z", "request_id": "req_011Cfbfvoy9vRSvyf538SP9N"}
